id of your lowest card efficiently while forcing the opponents to play higher cards to win the trick. Passing here would leave you with the 6, which would be very difficult to play out later without winning initiative first. Playing the Q is unnecessary overkill, and breaking your pairs (K or A) would ruin your hand\'s structure.\n\nReason: Playing the ♣6 is the most efficient move to clear a low card from the hand, preserving the strength of the high single Q and the pairs KK and AA.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♣6"]}'}
